## Reviewer got wrong (not applied)

- cs-a 3: article 10 on the withholding-rate link is what the English and Korean sources say.
  `flno=3` is a source-URL mismatch, not a Czech-only error. The statute name in Czech already
  follows the pcode. The digit was not changed.
- cs-a 18 and the "za poslední rok" / "dokončený rok" / "na přerušení" suggestions drop a
  source numeral. The checker has no Czech word for "one".
- cs-a 24 and cs-b 17: Q-lines are body blocks split by U+200B because the Korean source is.
  Making them headings or deleting the zero-width spaces fails blocks/headings.
- cs-a 39 and cs-b 27: a space as the thousands separator is the right Czech typography and
  the wrong checker convention. Dot grouping stays.
- cs-a 10's "dvě třetiny" and cs-b 26's "prvního pořadí" are more natural and were not used,
  for the same numeral reason. "2/3" and "1. pořadí" stay.
- cs-a 35's suggested sentence omitted "2". The self-reference is fixed without dropping it.
